-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Aug  2 16:56:46 UTC 2026 - Patrick Haar <Pihaar@users.noreply.github.com>

- Stationboard: fix the departure/arrival board so a selected platform
  shows its own departures from the initial view. At multi-platform
  stops (e.g. Wiesloch-Walldorf Bahnhof) the paging horizon, slice,
  line filter and load-more now operate on the platform-scoped board
  instead of the full station board, so the initial view is no longer
  empty when the next station-wide departure belongs to another
  platform, and the line filter matches what is shown. The scope
  decision is derived once (locL geometry, stable across reconciles
  and refetches) and shared by every consumer.
- Load-more now stays available at busy stops whose board hit the
  HAFAS 50-entry cap, as long as the selected platform has cached
  departures beyond the current horizon (the 50-cap hint no longer
  suppresses client-side pagination).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Aug  1 22:01:35 UTC 2026 - Patrick Haar <Pihaar@users.noreply.github.com>

- Fix the sysusers user creation at install time: reference the
  sysusers config via Source1 so %sysusers_create_package embeds it
  at build time. It previously read deploy/busradar-sysusers.conf from
  the not-yet-unpacked tarball, yielding an empty %pre and creating
  the busradar user only on the next boot.
- rpmlintrc: filter the renamed dir-or-file-outside-snapshot check
  for /opt/busradar and drop the stale non-standard-dir-in-usr filter.
- Track the /var/lib/busradar tmpfiles directory as %ghost.
